$\mathrm{I}=\int_0^\pi \frac{x \sin x}{1+\cos ^2 x} d x\qquad ....\mathrm{(i)}I=\int_0^\pi \frac{(\pi-x) \sin (\pi-x)}{1+\cos ^2(\pi-x)} d x=\int_0^\pi \frac{(\pi-x) \sin x}{\left.1+\cos ^2 x\right)} d x\qquad ....\mathrm{(ii)}$<br/>Adding (i) and (ii),
$2 \mathrm{I}=\int_0^\pi \frac{\pi \sin x}{1+\cos ^2 x} d x$<br/>Let $\cos x=t \Rightarrow-\sin x d x=d t\begin{aligned}
& 2 \mathrm{I}=\pi \int_{-1}^1 \frac{d t}{1+t^2} \\
& \Rightarrow 2 \mathrm{I}=\pi\left[\tan ^{-1}(t)\right]_{-1}^1 \Rightarrow \mathrm{I}=\frac{\pi^2}{4}
\end{aligned}$

$\left(x \sin \frac{y}{x}\right) d y=\left(y \sin \frac{y}{x}-x\right) d x\frac{d y}{d x}=\frac{y \sin \frac{y}{x}-x}{x \sin \frac{y}{x}} \Rightarrow \frac{d y}{d x}=\frac{y}{x}-\operatorname{cosec} \frac{y}{x}$<br/>Let $\frac{y}{x}=v \Rightarrow \frac{d y}{d x}=v+\frac{x d v}{d x}\begin{aligned}
& v+\frac{x d v}{d x}=v-\operatorname{cosec} v \\
& \frac{d v}{-\operatorname{cosec} v}=\frac{d x}{x} \Rightarrow-\sin v d v=\frac{d x}{x}
\end{aligned}$<br/>Integrating both side, we get $\cos v=\log x+\mathrm{C}\Rightarrow \cos \frac{y}{x}=\log x+C$

